WEBVTT

00:04:58.669 --> 00:05:01.005
NT: I've been doing this work
for about 25 years,

00:05:01.047 --> 00:05:02.548
one way or another,

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:04.133
in direct services at first

00:05:04.175 --> 00:05:06.635
and then in the policy work that Vera does

00:05:06.677 --> 00:05:08.095
and you know,

00:05:08.137 --> 00:05:11.474
I admit that I have seen
in the past five or six years

00:05:11.515 --> 00:05:14.101
that this has become
sort of a cause célèbre

00:05:14.143 --> 00:05:16.937
and people have gotten excited about it.

00:05:16.937 --> 00:05:19.815
I think that that is
a fundamentally good thing.

00:05:19.857 --> 00:05:21.984
If you remember
what I said a moment ago,

00:05:22.026 --> 00:05:25.988
that this is democracy
that created this monster that we have,

00:05:25.988 --> 00:05:30.451
and so the only way that we will undo it
is if people engage.